<h2>What Should Chase Cardholders Do?</h2>
<p>If you only have Chase Ultimate Rewards points and want to fly Cathay Pacific, there is a workaround: you can transfer your Chase points to British Airways Avios. Since both Cathay Pacific and British Airways are part of the oneworld alliance, you can use Avios to book Cathay Pacific award flights. Keep in mind that this is an indirect route. The mileage required via British Airways may differ from Asia Miles, and British Airways often passes on higher carrier-imposed surcharges for long-haul flights.</p>

<h2>How to Decide if a Transfer is Worth It</h2>
<p>Once you know the actual transfer ratio (e.g., 1:1 for Citi or 5:4 for Amex), the next step is calculating whether the resulting miles offer good value for the flight you want to book. Never guess—especially when transferring from Amex where you lose 20% upfront. Run the math to ensure the redemption is worth it.</p>

